    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Rigveda contains 10 Mandalas and 1,028 Suktas; the famous Gayatri Mantra is found in the 3rd Mandala.",
        "The Battle of Ten Kings (Dasrajna Yajna) took place on the banks of the Parushni (Ravi) river.",
        "Iron (referred to as Syamas or Krishna Ayas) was introduced in the Later Vedic Period around 1000 BCE.",
        "Indra (250 hymns) and Agni (200 hymns) are the two most frequently mentioned deities in the Rigveda."
      ],
